	(version 20240108)
	(generator "uwb_rescue_locator_lib_builder")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Fanstel BT840 (nRF52840) BLE module, 14 x 16 x 1.9 mm: 16 castellated pads (1-16) plus 49 LGA pads (Z0-Z6, A0-A6, B0-B6, C0-C6, D0-D6, E0-E6, F0-F6) = 65. Pad positions and sizes converted from Fanstel's own Eagle library BT840.lbr, package BT840 (fanstel.com/s/BT840.lbr, from fanstel.com/download-document) and cross-checked against Fanstel BT840/F/E/X/XE datasheet Ver 1.15 (Sep 2019) pp.9-10 mechanical drawings: castellated pitch 1.10 mm, LGA column pitch 1.50 mm, row pitch 1.20 mm, F0-F3 1.5 x 1.5 mm ground pads at 3.625/2.25 mm spacing, F6 0.6 x 0.6 mm square, round pads 0.6 mm. Pad names are the datasheet Pin Function table names (the Eagle names are P$1, P$A5 ...). Origin = body centre. PCB antenna occupies the top (pin 1/16 end is the antenna side of the castellations: the antenna region is y < -1.5 mm in this footprint); keep copper, battery and metal clear per datasheet p.16 (antenna should overhang the host board edge by 9.8 mm for best range).")
	(tags "Fanstel BT840 nRF52840 BLE module castellated LGA")
